er.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)={e}^{t}(\\,i+2\\,j+t\\,k)$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{t}\\,j+(t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{t})^{2}+({e}^{t}(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}({t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}(1+4+{t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,,4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(4-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widg