/verification.json"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+0+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\sqrt{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f739dfc10d723398afc82ce80c3319645e42094381b090dc46085d599a85f" "basis" 1766 "