"basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3063.json" "file_sha256" "c92f14e064fc67570e97c548727103230652186a36234e730b7b946cab910c7d" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3063.json" "file_sha256" "c92f14e064fc67570e97c548727103230652186a36234e730b7b946cab910c7d" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/29c97e5963d451cc389944ef113764b2d15998448e773a02bb98c062207c2860.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3064.json" "file_sha256" "aae1c10fbda307e8c5760f1441a9d730884b8f1469d948f741aaa6017649ceaa" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡2t+16{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3064.json" "file_sha256" "aae1c10fbda307e8c5760f1441a9d730884b8f1469d948f741aaa6017649ceaa" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/8573aedcd26cba038b2db072560cd3d6ba7676542888a2d9b8a356713eaf6724.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-6303.json" "file_sha256" "f326828e097bec933b49faf962a5b56f5ae069cf725d748e457efd34d13d2335" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\,t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-6303.json" "file_sha256" "f326828e097bec933b49faf962a5b56f5ae069cf725d748e457efd34d13d2335" "basis" 1766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-127427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{e}^{2t}+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-127427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/d42e9c6ed71f06c2dec273a91d3a4cfbdf5c58095be9370285d7987d38f7b5a6.png)\n\nWhich integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $h(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ from  $t=0$ to $t=2\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${h}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{h}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+1\\,k \\\\ ‖{h}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{h}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-64723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3-{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t+{t}^{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-33857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡2t-{sin}^{2}⁡2t+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $r(t)={t}^{3}\\,i+3t\\,j+{t}^{4}\\,k$ from  $t=2$ to $t=5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+3\\,j+4{t}^{3}\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(3)^{2}+(4{t}^{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+9+16{t}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-64724" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64724" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{8{t}^{5}+9{t}^{3}+6}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{{t}^{6}+{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-64724" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)={e}^{t}(\\,i+2\\,j+t\\,k)$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{t}\\,j+(t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{t})^{2}+({e}^{t}(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}({t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}(1+4+{t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+5}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/c4aa91668440687bbae4b1f85672f5cbaf7ce00d978049c7558eed99b7361d1a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t-{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-3{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3-3{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(6t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-18{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3({t}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+1-[\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)]) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}+1+\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-127585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/33412629fc30584cf4a1726eef7e4f23f623ae4439d25045d61e36f68914dacd.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+2)-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+2+\\frac{1}{3}+1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-127602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-77066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/9b83db0bb11b8e4bbcc4b04b7bf696879d4d7f4732d6aef7d005f9da2b625526.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨2{t}^{3/2},\\,3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-77066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\sqrt{t},\\,3⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{t})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9t+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3(t+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(t+1)^{3/2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-77066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-77066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mat