{0}^{3}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t)|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9+3-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+0+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\sqrt{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,3t,\\,4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}+(3t)^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{({t}^{2})}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+2)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({t}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+2t){|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}+2(0))-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+2(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fb3a5b9af65d21b9d95c7517a0a4f98cbb9e040a8b3d6e8b495d281fedc6ff97"} {"question" "q-127635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "q-127635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5e2344e2053875a8f7044cb31a6e2aa235174b1a4bf464f5f77a2d76c1d0fa0"} {"question" "e-3063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/example-3063.json" "file_sha256" "562bd65e556451f17de90f9bea227b6b7e2334fd6175016a977cd4aeafa236b3"} {"question" "e-3063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/example-3063.json" "file_sha256" "562bd65e556451f17de90f9bea227b6b7e2334fd6175016a977cd4aeafa236b3"} {"question" "e-3064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/29c97e5963d451cc389944ef113764b2d15998448e773a02bb98c062207c2860.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/example-3064.json" "file_sha256" "8ee0213fd2f9455b02d5ec99596a0eac62fcb2b40e528cea6e935cdf9cbe93c0"} {"question" "e-3064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡2t+16{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/example-3064.json" "file_sha256" "8ee0213fd2f9455b02d5ec99596a0eac62fcb2b40e528cea6e935cdf9cbe93c0"} {"question" "e-6303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/8573aedcd26cba038b2db072560cd3d6ba7676542888a2d9b8a356713eaf6724.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/example-6303.json" "file_sha256" "c7127bf8f18222f18054b7fb47fdd7cf1d911ca40f0fec9202b47952193ba959"} {"question" "e-6303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\,t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/example-6303.json" "file_sha256" "c7127bf8f18222f18054b7fb47fdd7cf1d911ca40f0fec9202b47952193ba959"}] "usage" {"e-6303" [] "e-3063" [] "q-77064" [] "q-76914" [] "e-3064" [] "q-33779" [] "q-77066" [] "q-127427" [] "q-33862" [] "q-76906" [] "q-77220" []} "basis" 2844 "retractions" [[17592186120455 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/q-77066.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g} ( t ) = \\langle  2 {t}^{3 / 2} , \\, 3 t \\rangle$ from $t = 0$ to $t = 3$."] [17592186120455 :question/worked-solution "Differentiate: $\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle3\\sqrt t,3\\rangle$, so the speed is $3\\sqrt{t+1}$. Therefore $$L=\\int_0^3 3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,dt=[2(t+1)^{3/2}]_0^3=2(8-1)=14.$$"] [17592186120455 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186330106 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$"] [17592186119486 :question/problem "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)"] [17592186119487 :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![